      "content": "Taking 99mg of potassium supplements without medical supervision is extremely risky for someone with Stage 3 kidney disease, as your kidneys may struggle to regulate excess levels, leading to life-threatening hyperkalemia. You should not start a new supplement regimen on your own; instead, please contact your nephrologist immediately to rule out other causes for your cramps and fatigue. They can accurately assess your current blood work and prescribe safe, kidney-appropriate potassium or alternative treatments specifically for you. Never adjust medication or dosages independently when managing chronic kidney disease.",
